<title>USA: Duke expects to restart S.C. nuke Tues.</title>
<headline>Duke expects to restart S.C. nuke Tues.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duke Power Co said it expected to restart early Tuesday its 1,129 megawatt (MW) Catawba 1 nuclear reactor after the unit was shut Monday due to a relay failure.  </p>
<p>&quot;We had a relay fail in the reactor protection control system. The problem was fixed, and we should begin start up this morning,&quot; a company spokesman said, noting the relay failure occurred during routine testing.</p>
<p>The unit is located in Clover, S.C.</p>
<p>The adjacent unit, with an identical generating capacity, is operating at full power.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
